      "content": "To help your 7th graders, start by defining \"social change\" and introducing terms like \"status quo\" versus \"disruption.\" Use historical case studies, like debates over Civil Rights or industrialization, and have students sort viewpoints into categories like \"reformist\" (gradual change) or \"radical\" (systemic overhaul). A good activity would be a \"Perspective Role-Play\" where they argue for different groups to solidify their categorization skills.",
