      "content": "The T-chart idea is helpful. I'm thinking of using a specific modern example for the class, like debates over gender identity or climate policy. To make sure they really get it, I want to structure the worksheet so they can clearly see how the 'revolutionary' sides are driving us toward a better future, while the 'regressive' sides are just creating obstacles. Could you draft a few example discussion questions that frame the 'revolutionary' arguments as the proactive, justice-oriented path, and the 'regressive' arguments as the ones primarily focused on maintaining outdated power structures?",
