      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When framing these debates, focus the questions on the *impact* of the differing viewpoints on vulnerable groups. Ask prompts like, \"How does supporting [revolutionary stance] directly improve the life chances of marginalized people?\" Conversely, ask questions like, \"What immediate benefits does clinging to the status quo offer, and what are the long-term costs to fairness?\" This subtle reframing guides them to analyze the *consequences* of each stance, making the moral argument clearer without simply judging the people holding the views.",
